# What must NOT enter the build context.
#
# On this project this is a SECURITY control, not a size optimisation. The build context is uploaded to
# the daemon and anything COPY'd is baked into a layer that survives every later deletion and travels
# with the image. Four of the entries below are the reason this file exists at all:
#
#   roster.json          children's real names (the only place they live at rest, ADR-0016)
#   auth-accounts.json   coaches' argon2id password hashes
#   data/                the raw telemetry store — children's location, plus the backups beside it
#   mosquitto/ft.passwd  broker credentials
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs an explicit list of files rather than `COPY . .`, so these are already excluded
# by construction; this file is the belt to that pair of braces, and it is also what keeps a stray
# `docker build` from shipping a 300 MB context.

node_modules
data
backups
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Secrets and personal data — never in an image.
roster.json
*roster*.json*
auth-accounts.json
*auth-accounts*.json*
auth-sessions.json
session-config.json
.env
.env.*
mosquitto/ft.passwd

# Not needed at runtime.
test
tsconfig.json
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.md
